{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Prepare for his sons.</b> Belshazzar and all his house:" "<b>For the iniquity of their fathers.</b> Evil-Merodach his father and Nebuchadnezzar his father's father:" "<b>Enemies.</b> Like ויהי עריך (1 Samuel 28:16). And the meaning is that he stirs up hatred in all the world. Now the meaning of ומלאו is that they shall not fill. And some say: after they do not inherit the earth, the world will be settled."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:49.837141579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}